WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.751 --> 00:00:02.044
You got good morals.

00:00:03.879 --> 00:00:05.255
What's good morals?

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:06.965
You know what
good morals is, bruv.

00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:11.720
It means you'll always
be there for your family…

00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:14.223
and for your brothers.

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:17.142
And you'll never
let them down.

00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:18.936
In this season of Top Boy,

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:21.438
many of the characters
are walking tightropes,

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:23.649
both outside and at home.

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:26.318
While some appear calm
on the surface,

00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:28.362
internally they're at war,

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:30.781
living lives
of quiet desperation.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.866
They are wrestling with
their own sense of morality

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.410
in a lifestyle
and a wider society

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:36.954
where empathy can cost

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.288
and even kill.

00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:41.375
Amid these tensions

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:43.752
and their long,
intense days,

00:00:43.836 --> 00:00:45.504
they try to find
their way through.

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:47.840
My name is Aniefiok
"Neef" Ekpoudom,

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:49.758
and in this video,
we'll be exploring

00:00:49.842 --> 00:00:51.635
right and wrong in Top Boy.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.642
In the early half
of the season,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.519
we're reunited with Sully.

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:02.479
He's at war with himself.

00:01:02.563 --> 00:01:04.940
After the traumas of seeing
Jason burn to death

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:06.108
in the previous season,

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:07.276
we find him

00:01:07.359 --> 00:01:09.486
as he is distancing himself
from the roads.

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:12.239
He moves into a barge
on the Thames,

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:15.117
slowly attempting to pull
his life back together,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.493
piece by piece,

00:01:16.577 --> 00:01:18.871
but those years
still haunt him.

00:01:19.413 --> 00:01:21.665
Fuck! Hey!

00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:24.877
-You're fucking early.
-My bad, bro.

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:28.046
He is seeking to recover
from the hangover of a life

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.132
where he lived on the edge
for so long.

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:32.926
But as Sully
peels back the layers

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.095
and tries to find space
to recover,

00:01:35.179 --> 00:01:37.431
he is forced to confront
his past actions.

00:01:37.973 --> 00:01:39.516
The guilt of murdering Dris

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.268
is eating at him
from the inside.

00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:43.979
You done Dris, didn't you?

00:01:44.855 --> 00:01:45.689
Come on.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.274
Don't know what the fuck
you're talking about.

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:49.234
Don't lie to me, man.

00:01:49.318 --> 00:01:50.444
You killed him.

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:52.362
Tell me you didn't kill him.

00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:53.989
Look me in my eyes

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:55.699
and tell me
that you didn't do it.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.117
Dris was my friend.

00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:58.952
That's not denying it,
is it?

00:01:59.036 --> 00:02:01.788
He scrambles to try
and make things right,

00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:03.207
easing the guilt he feels

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:06.126
by offering Mandy,
Dris's girlfriend, money.

00:02:06.752 --> 00:02:08.128
My life is different now.

00:02:08.754 --> 00:02:10.255
I don't want this.

00:02:10.339 --> 00:02:11.673
It's a cruel lesson:

00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:13.509
our actions can define us,

00:02:13.592 --> 00:02:16.178
the world may always see you
as who you once were,

00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:18.931
no matter how far
you try and outrun it.

00:02:19.014 --> 00:02:21.016
And so he must sit
with the consequences

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.601
of who he used to be.

00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:26.522
It's not a situation
unique to Sully.

00:02:27.231 --> 00:02:29.441
Throughout the season,
we find many of the youngers

00:02:29.525 --> 00:02:31.318
wrestling with
their own morality.

00:02:31.902 --> 00:02:33.529
Either through home traumas

00:02:33.612 --> 00:02:34.863
or life on the roads,

00:02:34.947 --> 00:02:36.198
they have suffered

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:37.699
and they're trying
to survive the day

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:39.243
the best way they know how.

00:02:39.326 --> 00:02:41.286
Cracks only appear
when they are confronted

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.413
by other members
of the community.

00:02:43.497 --> 00:02:45.123
I know what you make him do.

00:02:45.916 --> 00:02:47.876
You use him in the streets.

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:50.337
I know.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.214
I don't make him do nothing.

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:53.882
I don't know what
you're talking about, man.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.511
Jamie has an awareness
of that desperation,

00:02:57.594 --> 00:02:59.137
and it allows him
to show sympathy

00:02:59.221 --> 00:03:00.764
for the decisions Ats made.

00:03:00.848 --> 00:03:03.225
He recognises the vice
Ats was locked in,

00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:06.103
even if that vice cost Jamie
his own freedom

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.688
and tore him
from his family.

00:03:08.647 --> 00:03:10.649
He used to come here
and spend time with us,

00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:12.651
like watch TV with us,

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:15.320
eat with us, bro,
stay with Stef.

00:03:15.404 --> 00:03:16.738
You used to help Stef
with homework,

00:03:16.822 --> 00:03:18.490
help him with shit
that I couldn't, bro.

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:21.618
So I'll be real, like…

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.830
I'm not even trying
to hear that.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.333
Whatever he did…

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.460
what Dushane made him do…

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:33.505
the youth was family.

00:03:34.965 --> 00:03:36.925
Family is Jamie's
guiding light,

00:03:37.009 --> 00:03:38.302
his North Star.

00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:40.596
Everything he risks
is for them.

00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:42.014
And in their situation,

00:03:42.097 --> 00:03:44.474
where he is relied on
as the primary provider,

00:03:44.558 --> 00:03:47.936
any idea of what is
considered right or wrong

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.855
pales in significance

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:51.815
when the stakes
are Stef and Aaron.

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:53.609
I didn't ask for this…

00:03:54.568 --> 00:03:57.321
to be the mum and dad
to you and Stef.

00:03:58.739 --> 00:04:00.032
Fam, it's hard.

00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:02.784
Proper hard, bro.

00:04:05.913 --> 00:04:06.914
Man, for all of us.

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:11.543
I know you've been tryin',

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:13.670
and I've been tryin'.

00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:17.424
But I need you to know,
Aaron, yeah?

00:04:19.593 --> 00:04:21.720
Everything that I do…

00:04:23.931 --> 00:04:25.891
and all that I care about

00:04:26.475 --> 00:04:27.768
is the two of you.

00:04:29.478 --> 00:04:30.604
You and Stef,

00:04:31.188 --> 00:04:32.105
that's it.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.525
Ats was a foreshadowing,

00:04:34.608 --> 00:04:35.567
and before long

00:04:35.651 --> 00:04:37.653
the same desperation
that plagued Ats

00:04:37.736 --> 00:04:39.655
eventually confronts
Jamie too.

00:04:39.738 --> 00:04:41.281
He finds himself in a vice,

00:04:41.365 --> 00:04:43.158
either kill
his best friend Kit

00:04:43.242 --> 00:04:45.619
or uproot his siblings
and flee to Cardiff,

00:04:45.702 --> 00:04:47.162
costing Aaron his degree

00:04:47.246 --> 00:04:49.540
and Stef
any sense of stability.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.042
-He keeps true to mantra…
-Bro!

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.335
…prioritising family

00:04:53.418 --> 00:04:55.295
over anything
and everything.

00:04:55.379 --> 00:04:57.005
Hauntingly, that decision

00:04:57.089 --> 00:04:59.842
to look out for his siblings
over himself

00:04:59.925 --> 00:05:01.760
ultimately costs him
his life.

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:05.472
Jamie! Jamie!

00:05:05.556 --> 00:05:07.099
Jamie shows
that there is more here

00:05:07.182 --> 00:05:08.559
than the individual.

00:05:08.642 --> 00:05:11.854
Our actions never exist
in isolation or a vacuum.

00:05:12.896 --> 00:05:14.523
We are all products
of an environment,

00:05:14.606 --> 00:05:16.233
moulded by our surroundings.

00:05:16.859 --> 00:05:18.652
In Top Boy,
a coldness is threaded

00:05:18.735 --> 00:05:20.445
through the city
they inhabit,

00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:22.489
flowing from the top
downwards.

00:05:23.991 --> 00:05:25.033
This youth.

00:05:26.994 --> 00:05:28.078
One of ours.

00:05:31.123 --> 00:05:33.041
He got shanked up bad.

00:05:35.586 --> 00:05:37.004
Fourteen years old.

00:05:39.298 --> 00:05:42.217
Someone shanked
the life out of him,

00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:44.261
left him in a fucking skip.

00:05:44.887 --> 00:05:47.055
You believe that?
Like he meant nothing.

00:05:47.139 --> 00:05:49.933
First we see Amma,
Ats's mother,

00:05:50.017 --> 00:05:51.435
forced to leave the country

00:05:51.518 --> 00:05:53.478
while still grieving
for her murdered son.

00:05:53.562 --> 00:05:56.231
She's lived in this country
for 19 years.

00:05:56.315 --> 00:05:58.233
She's worked legally

00:05:58.317 --> 00:05:59.943
right up until you people
stopped her.

00:06:00.027 --> 00:06:01.862
She's paid her taxes,
she has rights.

00:06:01.945 --> 00:06:03.864
This woman has just lost
her one and only son

00:06:03.947 --> 00:06:05.866
to a devastating
knife crime.

00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:07.576
Are you aware of that?
Is that in your file?

00:06:07.659 --> 00:06:09.620
Can't you see this is wrong?

00:06:10.495 --> 00:06:14.249
Elsewhere, Summerhouse is
undergoing massive change.

00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:16.335
East London
is rapidly gentrifying.

00:06:16.418 --> 00:06:18.170
The tower blocks
are coming down

00:06:18.253 --> 00:06:20.005
and the residents
are being moved out.

00:06:20.839 --> 00:06:22.716
The looming forces
of the council

00:06:22.799 --> 00:06:24.051
and the private developers

00:06:24.134 --> 00:06:26.261
are squeezing out
the local community,

00:06:26.345 --> 00:06:28.514
tearing families
from their homes.

00:06:28.597 --> 00:06:31.183
Residents are rehoused
in far-flung places

00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:32.976
like Bolton and Croydon.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:35.854
And in an attempt to seize
the remaining properties,

00:06:35.938 --> 00:06:37.272
the developers
make life hell

00:06:37.356 --> 00:06:38.732
for the remaining residents.

00:06:39.983 --> 00:06:42.736
The developers treat them
as mere afterthoughts,

00:06:43.237 --> 00:06:45.197
minor obstructions
to the fruitful land

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.032
that they have been
living on for decades.

00:06:47.908 --> 00:06:49.159
Basic needs

00:06:49.243 --> 00:06:50.744
and any care
for human decency

00:06:50.827 --> 00:06:51.954
is stripped away

00:06:52.037 --> 00:06:54.873
as the developers ruthlessly
pursue the valuable land

00:06:54.957 --> 00:06:57.000
that sits under Summerhouse.

00:06:57.084 --> 00:06:59.294
I can't believe they're
making you guys still go.

00:07:00.546 --> 00:07:02.965
Do they know about
your mum's treatment?

00:07:03.048 --> 00:07:04.258
They know.

00:07:06.927 --> 00:07:08.303
Just don't give a shit.

00:07:08.387 --> 00:07:10.389
Nobody is more a product

00:07:10.472 --> 00:07:12.307
of their environment
than Dushane.

00:07:12.391 --> 00:07:14.059
He's grown up in Summerhouse

00:07:14.142 --> 00:07:15.853
and has seen
powerful institutions

00:07:15.936 --> 00:07:18.564
wielding the fate of
a community in their hands,

00:07:18.647 --> 00:07:21.024
reaching out and grabbing
for whatever they wish.

00:07:21.608 --> 00:07:22.985
And so he does the same,

00:07:23.068 --> 00:07:25.946
deciding to go for what
he wants by any means.

00:07:26.029 --> 00:07:29.116
Rather than trying to play
fair in an unfair world,

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:30.701
he adopts
their same behaviours.

00:07:30.784 --> 00:07:33.036
His decision to link up
with the developers

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.455
ultimately sees his
relationship with his mum

00:07:35.539 --> 00:07:37.040
come to a crisis point.

00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:39.168
Want me to be honest?

00:07:41.879 --> 00:07:42.880
I sell drugs.

00:07:44.548 --> 00:07:46.508
'Cause people
wanna get high.

00:07:46.592 --> 00:07:47.676
Everyone does it.

00:07:48.302 --> 00:07:51.138
And all of them politicians
you watch on the news,

00:07:53.056 --> 00:07:54.474
they all get high, you know.

00:07:54.558 --> 00:07:55.684
That's life.

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:57.144
That's how it goes.

00:07:57.227 --> 00:07:58.979
I mean, even the
Prime Minister was on TV

00:07:59.062 --> 00:08:01.231
talking about how someone
gave him drugs.

00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:03.108
Why ain't he in jail?

00:08:03.192 --> 00:08:05.027
That man has no morals.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:07.946
Don't try and use him
to justify what you do.

00:08:09.448 --> 00:08:11.742
I know you're using
the money you've made

00:08:11.825 --> 00:08:14.119
to tear down this community.

00:08:14.203 --> 00:08:16.371
Empathy and compassion
are a tightrope.

00:08:16.455 --> 00:08:18.040
And for a man like Sully,

00:08:18.123 --> 00:08:20.250
still half in and half out,

00:08:20.334 --> 00:08:22.169
we are shown
that love and understanding

00:08:22.252 --> 00:08:23.754
can be dangerous.

00:08:23.837 --> 00:08:26.465
Look, what it is,
Delphine, is…

00:08:28.175 --> 00:08:29.218
where I've been…

00:08:32.054 --> 00:08:33.889
people ain't really
that nice to you.

00:08:35.224 --> 00:08:37.142
When his niece, Pebbles
gets in trouble

00:08:37.226 --> 00:08:38.477
with a group from Peckham,

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.562
he feels himself slowly
being drawn back in.

00:08:41.522 --> 00:08:43.065
Them men ain't gonna
give a fuck!

00:08:44.525 --> 00:08:45.776
I know, I've been them!

00:08:47.277 --> 00:08:49.029
They is gonna want
their shit back.

00:08:49.112 --> 00:08:51.365
He starts to lose
who he was becoming,

00:08:51.448 --> 00:08:53.033
filtering back
into old ways.

00:08:53.116 --> 00:08:55.953
In confrontations,
he tries to show reason

00:08:56.036 --> 00:08:57.246
and a level of empathy,

00:08:57.329 --> 00:08:59.748
a new man in a world
that hasn't changed.

00:09:00.415 --> 00:09:01.708
First with Rashaun…

00:09:01.792 --> 00:09:02.876
-The fuck you doing?
-Pebbles!

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.087
You took something from her
that weren't hers to give,

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:06.964
but the people it belongs
to, they're fucking serious.

00:09:07.047 --> 00:09:08.590
And she might not have told…
Look at me!

00:09:09.258 --> 00:09:11.051
She might not have
told you that.

00:09:11.134 --> 00:09:12.553
'Cause she's fucking
sideways, I know.

00:09:14.596 --> 00:09:15.973
But I'm here being nice.

00:09:17.182 --> 00:09:18.225
They come…

00:09:19.643 --> 00:09:20.853
they ain't gonna be nice.

00:09:21.478 --> 00:09:23.397
And then with the group
in South London.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:24.940
After reason fails,

00:09:25.023 --> 00:09:26.233
he has to resort
to violence.

00:09:26.316 --> 00:09:27.901
What's wrong
with this silly boy?

00:09:29.278 --> 00:09:30.571
What's the point
in all this?

00:09:30.654 --> 00:09:32.781
I get it, you men are
fucking embarrassed.

00:09:33.365 --> 00:09:34.491
Pride and that.

00:09:35.576 --> 00:09:36.827
But neither work.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.579
In the end,
trying to bargain

00:09:38.662 --> 00:09:39.621
with the South London lot

00:09:39.705 --> 00:09:41.206
and doing a favour
for Pebbles

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.916
almost costs him his life.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.668
Love can get you killed.

00:09:44.751 --> 00:09:46.170
The incident changes him.

00:09:46.253 --> 00:09:49.173
He scrubs away the promise
of who he was becoming

00:09:49.256 --> 00:09:50.632
and falls back
into his old self.

00:09:50.716 --> 00:09:52.634
As the compassion
withers away,

00:09:52.718 --> 00:09:55.220
a ruthlessness emerges
in its place,

00:09:55.304 --> 00:09:56.305
and it culminates with him

00:09:56.388 --> 00:09:58.515
murdering Jamie
in front of Stef.

00:09:59.349 --> 00:10:00.851
It was a defining moment

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:03.353
for one of the most troubled
characters in the series.

00:10:03.437 --> 00:10:05.939
The promise of what he
could have been is gone,

00:10:06.023 --> 00:10:07.274
lost to the darkness.

00:10:07.357 --> 00:10:10.068
Dushane is also changed
by a traumatic event.

00:10:10.611 --> 00:10:11.612
His mum passes away

00:10:11.695 --> 00:10:13.280
while he is out
on the roads.

00:10:13.363 --> 00:10:16.158
Distraught by her death,
he almost collapses.

00:10:16.241 --> 00:10:17.910
Eventually,
he heeds the words

00:10:17.993 --> 00:10:19.536
of their final conversation

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:21.205
and steps in
to secure the future

00:10:21.288 --> 00:10:22.789
of the community
in Summerhouse.

00:10:22.873 --> 00:10:24.833
You gotta change the plans
back to the way they were.

00:10:24.917 --> 00:10:26.001
Tell mum,

00:10:26.835 --> 00:10:27.961
she used to say…

00:10:28.921 --> 00:10:30.839
"Summerhouse is
more than numbers."

00:10:30.923 --> 00:10:32.633
It's a subtle shifting
of the dial.

00:10:32.716 --> 00:10:34.134
By the end of the season,

00:10:34.218 --> 00:10:35.761
both him and Sully

00:10:35.844 --> 00:10:38.347
have inched slightly away
from who they once were,

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:39.640
and Jamie has gone.

00:10:40.349 --> 00:10:41.725
The season is an observation

00:10:41.808 --> 00:10:44.853
of how young people caught
in desperate circumstances

00:10:44.937 --> 00:10:47.064
wrestle with morality
and empathy,

00:10:47.147 --> 00:10:49.024
sometimes to
their own detriment.

00:10:49.107 --> 00:10:50.400
We are shown
that there are dangers

00:10:50.484 --> 00:10:51.568
for doing the right thing,

00:10:51.652 --> 00:10:53.111
but also freedom.

00:10:54.905 --> 00:10:56.073
You do what you have to

00:10:56.156 --> 00:10:58.200
to protect the people
that you love.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:02.829
The people you care about,
your family.

00:11:03.455 --> 00:11:04.873
And I love you for that.

